# Alternative to `python -m src.main --schedule`: let the OS scheduler call a one-shot command each hour.
# The pipeline is idempotent per hour and protected by a database lock, so a late or doubled trigger is safe.
#
# Slots are IST hours. IST = UTC+05:30, so the top of an IST hour is minute 30 on a UTC server clock.
# (If the machine clock is set to IST, use minute 0 and minute 50 instead.)
# Linux/macOS crontab on a UTC machine (run at IST top-of-hour, check at +20 minutes):
30 * * * *  cd /path/to/ajio-visibility-pipeline && .venv/bin/python -m src.main --run-once --trigger scheduled
50 * * * *  cd /path/to/ajio-visibility-pipeline && .venv/bin/python -m src.main --check-completeness
#
# Windows Task Scheduler (local time = IST: start at hh:00, repeat every 1 hour):
#   Program: C:\path\to\ajio-visibility-pipeline\.venv\Scripts\python.exe
#   Arguments: -m src.main --run-once --trigger scheduled
#   Start in:  C:\path\to\ajio-visibility-pipeline
